3. She takes iron supplements to manage her anemia but avoids taking them with tea. (Verbatim: "I'm gonna make sure I take my iron tablets... not right now though because I'm drinking my morning cup of tea.")

4. She grew up in a household with thin walls, where her parents (Mama and Papa Elia) would react angrily to her weekend alarms. (Verbatim: "the house I grew up in with Mama and Papa Elia had very thin walls... I would get shouted out for my alarm [on weekends].")

5. She associates alarm clock noises with stress and panic, a reaction developed from childhood experiences. (Verbatim: "I think I've been raised to have a natural panic when I hear an alarm clock... it's the same kind of panic you see in my horror game streams.")

6. She once lived in the jungle for research purposes under harsh conditions, including no electricity, outdoor living, and dangerous wildlife. (Verbatim: "my peak stress point was... when I was doing my research in the jungle living feral with like no electricity... accidentally sleeping with a snake... chased by the giant monkey.")

