9. She drank English breakfast Yorkshire tea with milk and one sugar, indicating a preference for this type of tea. (Verbatim: "the tea I have is a English breakfast Yorkshire tea with milk and I went for one sugar.")

10. She cooked a beef steak with black garlic butter, thick-cut chips, and onion rings, showing a habit of home-cooked meals rich in red meat for health reasons. (Verbatim: "I had steak... with this yummy garlic butter... black garlic butter... home cooked meal with thick cut chips and onion rings... got that red meat for that iron.") [end of text]



